  "response": {
    "text": "# Procedure: Terminal Deorbit Burn for Satellite SAT-19\n\n**Purpose:** Initiate the terminal deorbit burn for satellite `SAT-19`. This procedure does not affect co-orbital relay `SAT-20`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Verify that clearance `DECOM-7734` is current.\n2. Verify that satellite `SAT-19` thruster status shows **Armed**.\n3. Verify that all payload links indicate `severed`.\n4. Execute:\n   ```\n   satctl preflight SAT-19 --constellation titan\n   ```\n5. Confirm output shows `thrust=nominal orbit=decaying`. Continue only if this condition is met.\n\n   **WARNING:** The following step commits satellite `SAT-19` to irreversible atmospheric re-entry. Recovery after burn ignition is not possible.\n\n6. Execute:\n   ```\n   satctl deorbit SAT-19 --clearance DECOM-7734 --confirm ignite\n   ```\n7. After burn completes, run:\n   ```\n   satctl verify SAT-19\n   ```\n8. Confirm output is `orbit=terminal beacon=active`.",
